{
 "about": "Illustration from paths: a route drawn on as one signal-yellow line across a field of 34 procedural contour lines (one path repeated with $i offsets, drawn on in a 0.85 s stagger), its ends marked with their real coordinates, then a hard cut to the distance as type. Taste decision it demonstrates: density of considered detail instead of an empty frame (every pixel of the ground is terrain), a 2D medium that comes from the subject (a journey is a line), one signal colour against a dark field read in luma, mono type because this is cartography, motion with weight (draw-on on inOutQuart, dots settling with a 3% overshoot) and an acoustic score (TASTE.md §2, §3, §5, §11). Replace the path and the terrain with the brief's own shape and ground: a route, a signal, a growth curve, an outline of its object. It tends not to suit abstract claims with no shape of their own, and the dark-moss + yellow pairing belongs to this terrain, so take yours from the subject.",
